 "_note": "The authoritative mixed-precision basis for AGENTS.md's acceptance thresholds. Three caveats, all visible in the data. (1) The GPU is an NVIDIA L4, not the T4 the guide assumes -- Colab allocates whatever is free -- so the thresholds are named for the L4. (2) CUDA still failed with CUDA_ERROR_UNSUPPORTED_PTX_VERSION on all three precisions, so the basis is OpenCL/mixed rather than CUDA/mixed; both are genuine mixed precision, but OpenMM's CUDA and OpenCL platforms are separate implementations and CUDA remains unmeasured. (3) OpenCL/mixed and OpenCL/single report bit-identical single-point forces, which is expected rather than suspicious: OpenMM's `mixed` computes forces in single and only accumulates the integration in double, so the two differ in the NVE drift (-0.0235 against +0.0479) and not in a single-point force."
}